From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 21:51:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/24] script: implement isPointInFill, isPointInStroke and
 getPointAtLength

The rest of the cheap half of Phase 0. All three were commented out in
the WebIDL, and all three are nearly free now: the hit-testing module
already answers point-in-fill and point-in-stroke, and kurbo's
inv_arclen gives point-at-length by walking segments rather than
flattening the path.

Point queries are in the element's own user space, so no transform is
involved. isPointInStroke ignores dashes, matching hit_test: a dashed
stroke is one region, not a row of them. getPointAtLength clamps
distances outside the path to its ends.

pathLength deliberately does not scale either length API. It calibrates
distance-along-path for rendering -- dashes, markers, textPath -- not
for the DOM. I had this backwards in a comment and the code right;
svg/types/scripted/SVGGeometryElement.getTotalLength-01.svg settles it
by setting pathLength="1000" on a 200-unit path and asserting 200. The
comment now cites the test.

svg/ WPT: +287 subtests against the pref-off baseline, zero regressions,
up from +212. 52 unit tests.

Two of the tests that exercise these APIs still do not pass, for reasons
outside this patch. The .svg ones are standalone SVG documents, which
take a path native SVG never sees, and they errored before this too.
getTotalLength-02.html needs width.baseVal.value -- SVGAnimatedLength,
which is Phase 0's remaining half.
